    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-upside production today, headlined by the middle infield duo of **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.57). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive 14% park boost and a soft matchup against Sugano; his elite efficiency metrics make him an auto-start despite the high-stakes Roto environment. We are also leaning heavily into the speed and order advantages of **Henry Bolte** (65.40) and **Nasim Nunez** (61.05). **Henry Bolte** benefits from an aggressive matchup against Bradford, and given our focus on stealing bases to bolster our standing, his presence atop the order is vital. While **Kyle Tucker** (50.13) occupies a lineup spot, his low score is a byproduct of facing the elite 2.71 xERA of Mautz; he remains a start based on his pedigree, but he is our most vulnerable asset today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Heliot Ramos** (49.25), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Luis Lara** (50.14) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.10). While **Heliot Ramos** offers the high-end sprint speed we covet, the projection system favored the consistency of **Miguel Vargas** in the #3 spot against Wesneski. We also considered **Wade Meckler** (40.71), but his score was cannibalized by a tough matchup against the 2.96 xERA of Schlittler. We continue to monitor **Andy Pages**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while keeping an eye on **Liam Hicks**, whose 38.31 score fell below our mandatory 40-point efficiency floor.\n\nWe enter the slate with a cautious eye on **Kyle Tucker**, whose matchup against Mautz presents the highest risk of a sub-optimal day. Conversely, **Luis Robert Jr.** (68.84) is a prime candidate for a breakout; despite a dynamic platoon disadvantage of -15%, the massive park and SP skill factors are dragging his projection upward. **Drake Baldwin** (56.92) is our primary indicator for the day\u2014if his #1 spot in the order translates to early run production, we should successfully navigate the matchups against tougher arms like Lord and Sugano. We are fully committed to this configuration, prioritizing high-velocity baserunners like **Nasim Nunez** and **Henry Bolte** to maintain our competitive edge in the SB category.",
